# ── MARK LIII — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
# Git does not allow a comment after a pattern on the same line: the text becomes
# part of the pattern and the rule silently matches nothing. So every comment sits
# on its own line above the pattern it describes.

# Your Gemini API key, plus per-plugin credentials (Alpaca paper keys included)
config/api_keys.json
# The dashboard's TLS private key and certificate
config/certs/
# A LINKED WhatsApp session. Committing it hands somebody your WhatsApp account,
# not just a key
config/whatsapp_web/
# Google OAuth tokens (Gmail / Calendar plugins)
**/token*.json
# Google OAuth client secrets
**/client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
config/gmail_token.json
config/gmail_token.json.tmp
config/gmail_*_token.json
config/gmail_*_token.json.tmp
# Private promotion drafts, contacts, and opt-outs
config/product_sales/
# Paper-trading journal, state and runner log (numbers only)
config/trading/
config/trading_day/
.env
.env.*

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/*.db
# Runtime lock files (for example Mission Control's)
memory/*.lock

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/
